hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28197","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr and Surayj, the meaning, said: Nafi ibn Umar meaning al-Jumahi narrated to us, on the authority of Umayyah ibn Safwan, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr. He said: My father, both of them said: on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say at al-Nabaah or al-Nabawah, Nafi ibn Umar doubted, of Taif, while he says: O people, you are about to know the people of Paradise from the people of Fire, or he said: your best from your worst. He said: A man of the people said: By what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By bad praise and good praise, and you are witnesses of Allah, some of you upon others."
